Provides: gtkdialog
Replaces: gtkdialog
Description: GTK3 dialog window creator for shell scripts
 gtk3dialog builds GTK3 dialog windows from an XML-like description
 language, allowing shell scripts to display interactive GUI windows without
 knowledge of any graphical toolkit. This is the haplo-dialog fork
 (1.0.0) with security hardening (safe_exec, FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE,
 Full RELRO, stack-protector-strong).
 .
 Under Wayland, a window can be anchored as a wlr-layer-shell surface (bar,
 dock, desktop widget) with the layer, edge and dist attributes; elsewhere
 those attributes are ignored and an ordinary window is shown.
 .
 Toolkit: GTK3 — haplo-dialog fork 1.0.0.
 Security: safe_exec (no system()), FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
 stack-protector-strong.
